# tools/font5x7_boxdiag_witness.rish -- the open diagonal box-drawing corpus proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) - the third content BEYOND printable ASCII for the open glyph atlas
# image/glyph.rye (gfa1), completing the box-drawing family beside the light set (tools/font5x7_box_witness.rish,
# U+2500..U+253C) and the double set (tools/font5x7_boxdouble_witness.rish, U+2550..U+256C).
#
# The crux this witness proves is a REAL, OPEN, hand-drawn diagonal box corpus: the three light diagonal marks --
# the forward slash, the backslash, and their cross -- at their real Unicode codepoints U+2571..U+2573, each a 5x7
# coverage grid drawn in the open as ASCII line art in image/font5x7_boxdiag.rye, built into a gfa1 atlas and proven
# on metal. These are the marks a terminal surface (the Dexter/Scooter family) reaches for to strike through a cell,
# hatch a region, or mark an X. A full round-trip recovers every codepoint, advance, and coverage byte byte-for-byte;
# all three marks look up present and carry the shared advance while an ASCII letter misses; no two marks share
# coverage; the cross is exactly the two single diagonals overlaid (a union); and each mark reads within an honest
# legibility band. Compression is reported as a fact, never asserted -- the round-trip is the proof. No network, no
# key, no funds -- the marks a surface reads the day it wants to hatch or cross a cell, on our own open font.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/font5x7_boxdiag_witness.rish

say "font5x7-boxdiag: Language EN -- Season G's third font content beyond ASCII; the three light diagonal box marks drawn in the open as ASCII line art, built into the gfa1 atlas, completing the box family the light and double sets began."
say "font5x7-boxdiag: Style Radiant -- the drawings are the specification and the bytes are derived from them, so decode(encode(atlas)) recovers every mark byte for byte; our own hand, permissively ours, no external font to license and no web-search gate."
say "font5x7-boxdiag: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, u8 coverage bytes; every buffer names a maximum (cell_area - boxdiag_count - the atlas ceilings it rests on); each function states its invariants positively; codepoints explicit and strictly ascending; the source stays plain ASCII with numeric codepoints though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range; the cross-is-a-union property asserted, compression a reported fact; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/font5x7_boxdiag"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/font5x7_boxdiag.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "font5x7-boxdiag: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "font5x7-boxdiag: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "font5x7-boxdiag: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-font5x7-boxdiag" else "font5x7-boxdiag: selftest did not print the GREEN corpus line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trip byte-identical" else "font5x7-boxdiag: round-trip was not byte-identical"

assert selftest.out contains "the cross is exactly the two single diagonals overlaid" else "font5x7-boxdiag: the cross was not proven the union of the two single diagonals"

say "font5x7-boxdiag: GREEN -- the open diagonal box corpus whole; three light marks round-trip byte-identical, all present, distinct, legible, and the cross is the union of the two single diagonals; the box-drawing family is complete."
